{
  "id": 270337402,
  "iid": 13702,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "QUIC: Handle Connection Migrations",
  "description": "In Quic Connection Migrations are possible even without Client\nConnection IDs. Currently, after Connection Migration Wireshark fails to\nassociate answers to the new address to the original connection.\n\nSo if a migration happens and the client sends data from the new IP\nthe connection data needs to be associated with the new conversation.\nSo when the server answers and the connection is identified by the\nconversation, a connection is found.\n\nSince I'm not really familiar with the Wireshark source code nor with all details from the quic rfcs. I'm really happy to get any feedback :smile:\n\nDuplicate of https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/13693",
  "state": "merged",
