        {
          "id": 1696442919,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Ah, good catch. Yes, I suppose we can't call it necessarily non-conforming from Wireshark's perspective because of middleboxes (though if the client is doing it without a middlebox being involved, it is still nonconforming I reckon.)\n\nIt does seem like the two sides are doing the proper path validation with the PATH CHALLENGE and PATH RESPONSE, so that's good.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
