        {
          "id": 1697638661,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Thanks again.\n\nBTW, a tip, something you can do in 4.2.0:\n\nLoad the pcapng.\nConfigure the sslkeylog file so things are decrypted.\nFrom the Wireshark menus, select Edit->Inject TLS Secrets\nFile->Save\n\nThe file will now have the TLS secrets used for encrypting (but only those used in the file, not other ones from the keyfile) embedded in the pcapng as a Decryption Secrets Block. (If the file is not originally pcapng, you can do this and then \"Save As\" a pcapng.)\n\nTo remove a DSB, there's a similar \"Edit->Discard All Secrets\" option. Both of them make the filename be followed by a \"*\" in the titlebar, and will warn of unsaved changes if you quit. (It doesn't warn yet about saving in a non-pcapng format that doesn't support storing the secrets, though.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
