    {
      "id": "16da5948cf2f2b241d5acfd9c2750d4c475bf4ff",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1696253845,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Interesting, so our client on top of Google quiche is not RFC conforming :smile:.\n\nIs Wireshark handling RFC conforming Quic Migrations?\nFrom the Quic dissector code I've seen so far, New Connection IDs are not added to `quic_info_data` (connection) or a new entry created since it is indexed by the connection ID.\n\nOr is there a mechanism in the GUI to link two UDP Connections together?\n\nThanks for the feedback!",
          "author": {
            "id": 3800858,
            "username": "schrc3b6",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Max",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c45a6f7c111a8642aac101b228ae88006fe297a8164b91e988e026cf2fed7d28?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/schrc3b6"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-12-15T11:49:01.079Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-12-20T15:12:32.223Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 270337402,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2023-12-20T15:12:32.223Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 13702,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1696348032,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> Is Wireshark handling RFC conforming Quic Migrations? From the Quic dissector code I've seen so far, New Connection IDs are not added to quic_info_data (connection) \n\nTheoretically, [yes](epan/dissectors/packet-quic.c#L2614-2618):\n\n```c\n            quic_cid_t cid = {.len=0};\n            if (valid_cid && quic_info) {\n                tvb_memcpy(tvb, cid.cid, offset, nci_length);\n                cid.len = nci_length;\n                cid.seq_num = seq_num;\n                quic_connection_add_cid(quic_info, &cid, from_server);\n            }\n```\n\nIn practice, I don't know that we have gotten many samples of RFC conforming migrations so it's hard to say if it works or not. :grin: \n\n> Or is there a mechanism in the GUI to link two UDP Connections together?\n\nIdeally, there would be a table in the Conversations window that would have stats for an entire QUIC connection, across migration. That doesn't happen yet.\n\nYou can filter with the `quic.connection.number` generated field in the tree, which is what should eventually be used for the Conversations window.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-12-15T12:40:10.493Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-12-20T15:12:32.223Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 270337402,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2023-12-20T15:12:32.223Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 13702,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1696385955,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> In practice, I don't know that we have gotten many samples of RFC conforming migrations so it's hard to say if it works or not.\n\nI will do some testing to see if this also happens when a different CID is used after connection migration, and provide some pcaps :smile:",
          "author": {
            "id": 3800858,
            "username": "schrc3b6",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Max",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/c45a6f7c111a8642aac101b228ae88006fe297a8164b91e988e026cf2fed7d28?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/schrc3b6"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-12-15T13:02:20.728Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-12-20T15:12:32.223Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 270337402,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
